# DIAspeXtract: three changes to OpenMS ElutionPeakDetection.
#
# 1. Make detectPeaks(vector) lock-free for nested parallel callers.
#
# It guarded a shared output vector with a PROGRAM-GLOBAL named critical. Called from inside
# DIAspeXtract's per-band trace loop (96 concurrent callers) that one lock serialised the whole
# tool: 195M context switches, 37% system time. At top level this now collects into per-thread
# buffers and merges; when already nested it runs serially into the caller's own vector. No output
# vector is ever shared across threads, so the critical is unnecessary. Numerically identical:
# verified 1,528,113 spectra / 10,036 peptides identical across two machines.
#
# 2. Cache the Savitzky-Golay filter coefficients per thread.
#
# smoothData() constructed a SavitzkyGolayFilter and called setParameters() on every mass trace,
# and updateMembers_() recomputes the coefficients with one Eigen SVD per half-window on every
# such call. The coefficients depend only on (frame_length, polynomial_order), which take a
# handful of distinct values in a run, while smoothData() is called hundreds of millions of times.
# Caching the configured filter in a thread_local map leaves the coefficients, the filtering loop
# and every float conversion untouched. Measured on a 30-minute acquisition, with the two callers
# unchanged: MS1 tracing CPU 411 -> 228 s (-44%), the window loop 10,132 -> 9,105 CPU s (-10%),
# total CPU -11%, spectrum list byte-identical.
#
# 3. An optional fixed scan time for the smoothing window (param "scan_time", 0 = as before).
#
# win_size = chrom_fwhm / mt.getAverageMS1CycleTime(): a trace's own average cycle time is
# inflated by its gaps when the caller hands over real points only, so a long gappy trace gets a
# narrower window than its neighbours, and a sub-range of it (an RT tile) is smoothed and split
# differently from the whole. A caller that knows the acquisition's frame spacing passes it; the
# default reproduces the old behaviour byte for byte.
#
# Base: OpenMS/OpenMS develop bd4b89555629d68b431b189a4c841efbcc4dfeea (2026-04-24).
# Regenerated 2026-09-09 against that commit; verified to reproduce the built tree byte-for-byte.
--- a/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/ElutionPeakDetection.cpp
+++ b/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/ElutionPeakDetection.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
